change:
  id: CHG-033
  title: A fixture with more than one good answer
  status: proposed
  intent: Give a generation something to rank. The toy fixture has one correct edit, so every passing candidate scores the same and spread is zero by construction (ADR-0002 First measurement). A second fixture has several distinct edits that pass every required case, with held-out cases that reward different improvements, so distinct good candidates score differently.
  audience_level: developer
  relates_to:
    - ADR-0002
    - RISK-010
    - PAT-004

deltas:
  - op: ADDED
    capability: mutation-fitness-loop
    requirement: The repository ships fixtures/multi-answer-workflow, a target where at least three distinct edits each pass every required behaviour case and earn different held-out results, and where enough cases are declared that one held-out failure keeps a candidate above the promotion threshold.
    scenarios:
      - id: S1
        when: the baseline is checked
        then: at least one required case fails, so a run shows a DISCARD-to-PROMOTE transition
      - id: S2
        when: each of the reference answers in the fixture is applied and checked
        then: every one passes all required cases, their held-out results differ, and their fitness scores differ
      - id: S3
        when: a reference answer that fails exactly one held-out case is scored
        then: it still promotes, so the fixture does not trip RISK-010
      - id: S4
        when: a live model writes a good value with different case, spacing or a listed synonym, or writes a disabled, empty or repeated value
        then: the good spelling passes the check and the disabled, empty or repeated value fails it

acceptance:
  - scenario: S1
    test_id: cli/MultiAnswerFixtureAcceptanceTest.theBaselineFailsARequiredCase
    layer: acceptance
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: cli/MultiAnswerFixtureAcceptanceTest.everyReferenceAnswerPassesTheGatesAndTheyScoreDifferently
    layer: acceptance
  - scenario: S3
    test_id: cli/MultiAnswerFixtureAcceptanceTest.oneHeldOutFailureStillPromotes
    layer: acceptance
  - scenario: S4
    test_id: cli/MultiAnswerFixtureAcceptanceTest.checksAcceptPlausibleSpellingsAndRejectDisabledOrRepeatedValues
    layer: acceptance

tasks:
  - id: T1
    slice: Fixture files, reference answers and README
    status: completed
  - id: T2
    slice: Acceptance test running saaa-evolve on each reference answer with real Git and checks
    status: completed
  - id: T3
    slice: README fixture section and ADR-0002 (both copies) name the fixture as the population target
    status: completed

non_goals:
  - a live-model run; that is a measurement, recorded after merge
  - changing the scorer or RISK-010
  - changing the toy fixture

risks:
  - Hand-picked reference answers prove the fixture can separate candidates, not that a model will find different ones.
  - The weakest answer (tests-only, and the canned mutation) clears the threshold by about 0.033. Adding a case it fails, or a larger diff, can drop it below 0.80; the fixture README states the margin.
  - The checks accept listed synonyms only. A model's spelling outside them fails for wording rather than intent; workflow.txt lists the canonical values so the model can see them.
